irst time we're  hearing from his attorney Colburn and  his wife Amy are accused of paying  singers foundation 25 thousand dollars  to have a Proctor take the SATs for  their son their apparent admission  recorded you know  wiretap conversation with singer but  their attorney tells CBS News their son  took the test himself and says there's  no evidence the proctor corrected his  answers I don't think it's fair to say  that this case is a slam dunk even  though they have an insider  he's a vulnerable insider and those  wiretaps what we know now may not tell  the whole story  now Yale is officially the first goal to  wristed admission to a student connected  to this whole scheme many of the parents  are going to be here in court this week  but also next week in two of the highest  profile defendants of the case will be  in court next week that's actress Lorie  Lachlan and Felicity Huffman Gayle all  right Carter thank you very much
 

